Components Used

1. Arduino Nano
Acts as the main microcontroller. It reads sensor inputs, processes the line-following logic, and controls the motors through the motor driver.

2. IR Sensor Array Module (5-Channel)
Used to detect the black line on the surface. Each IR sensor provides digital output based on line position, helping the robot decide direction.

3. Motor Driver Module (L298N / TB6612FNG type)
Interfaces between the Arduino Nano and the DC motors. It allows control of motor direction and speed using digital and PWM signals.

4. DC Gear Motors (2x)
Provide motion to the robot wheels. One motor controls the left wheel and the other controls the right wheel.

5. Robot Wheels (2x)
Mounted on the DC motors to enable smooth movement of the robot.

6. Battery (Lithium-ion / AA Battery Pack)
Supplies power to the Arduino, motor driver, and motors.

7. Push Buttons (2x)
Used for user input, such as starting or stopping the robot and changing modes.

8. Jumper Wires (Male-to-Male / Male-to-Female)
Used to make electrical connections between the Arduino, sensors, motor driver, buttons, and power source.

9. Chassis / Base Plate
Provides mechanical support for mounting all components securely.

10. Power Switch (Optional)
Used to turn the power supply ON or OFF.
